    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d13">

                <pb facs="0092" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d13-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Excerpts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-10-22">22 October 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 632, Personal and Top Secret, from the President to the Prime
                    Minister.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The selection of a Black Sea port for our next meeting seems to be dependent upon
                    our ability to get through the Dardanelles safely as I wish to proceed by ship.
                    Do you think it is possible to get U. J. to come to Athens or Cyprus?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d13-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d13-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
